          "result": {
            "answer": {
              "id": "Ab013e64530",
              "markdown": "None of the products appear in both rankings: the top five revenue generators and top five products by customer count share zero overlap [E1]. This separation illustrates that in Q1 2026, top-line revenue and customer reach were driven by different dynamics: highest-revenue items generated between 216.00 and 259.99 from only 1 to 2 customers each (high revenue per customer, ranging from 108.00 to 259.99), whereas the widest-reach items attracted 2 to 3 customers each but yielded lower total revenue (40.00 to 208.50, or 20.00 to 69.50 per customer) [E1]. Because unit sales and individual price points are not measured here, whether this divergence stems from higher individual retail prices or multiple units purchased per buyer remains an unverified possibility.",
